WEBVTT

00:08.800 --> 00:10.530
(Murderer! Die!)

00:10.530 --> 00:12.280
(Turn Yourself In)

00:12.280 --> 00:14.640
(Trash Family)

00:17.700 --> 00:19.500
(Get Lost! Vampire)

00:19.500 --> 00:21.290
We tried our best, but it was no use.

00:23.320 --> 00:24.270
That girl

00:24.890 --> 00:26.380
is a spawn of evil.

00:35.290 --> 00:36.300
(Himiko, 3 years old. Himiko, 2 years old)
Stop.

00:37.040 --> 00:38.360
(Trash! Piece of Trash!)
Your Quirk

00:38.360 --> 00:40.310
(Go to Hell)
can never be accepted by society.

00:40.890 --> 00:42.800
No one can live however they please.

00:46.430 --> 00:48.860
(Atone for Your Sins with Your Life)
Himiko's face is so scary!

00:50.220 --> 00:51.510
You must endure.

00:52.270 --> 00:55.200
(Vampires! Die and Repent!)
We are saying this for your own good!

00:58.020 --> 00:59.310
(Murderer! Vampire!)

01:03.680 --> 01:05.390
I want to be a little bird.

01:06.110 --> 01:08.810
I want to sing and hop around.
It's so cute.

01:09.530 --> 01:11.050
I want to become Kei.

01:11.530 --> 01:13.870
Those dimples
when she smiles are so lovely.

01:15.040 --> 01:17.040
I dream every night.

01:17.770 --> 01:19.980
I dream of a dancing red sparrow.

01:20.460 --> 01:22.940
It's tap-dancing on my tummy.

01:23.440 --> 01:25.790
It eventually rips my tummy open

01:26.140 --> 01:28.140
and starts dancing inside my body.

01:28.960 --> 01:31.530
It stains me crimson red.

01:31.980 --> 01:34.700
It's so cute.

01:35.720 --> 01:37.500
That's a nice dream.

01:38.040 --> 01:39.230
Such a happy dream.

01:46.190 --> 01:48.360
Everything was thrown away.

01:52.730 --> 01:54.890
Even a lunatic like you

01:55.370 --> 01:58.170
can get sentimental, huh?

01:58.860 --> 02:01.230
I was just curious about the old home.

02:01.550 --> 02:02.780
That is perfectly normal, okay?

02:04.010 --> 02:05.450
Have you made up your mind?

02:05.880 --> 02:07.120
About what?

02:07.800 --> 02:10.990
About ending
this hopelessly corrupt world.

02:10.990 --> 02:12.430
Do you even have to ask?

02:12.430 --> 02:13.580
Not bad.

02:14.120 --> 02:16.540
Cries or laughter,

02:16.540 --> 02:18.570
tomorrow comes for all of us.

02:19.130 --> 02:20.090
In that case,

02:20.730 --> 02:21.880
let's have a good laugh,

02:22.200 --> 02:23.180
Himiko Toga.

02:23.550 --> 02:24.520
Humans

02:26.010 --> 02:28.000
should live to laugh!

02:33.160 --> 02:35.340
Someone might spot this, Toya.

02:37.690 --> 02:38.890
You're so kind.

02:39.420 --> 02:43.200
The authority doesn't
have the manpower to hunt us down.

02:43.660 --> 02:45.200
I'm being kind

02:45.200 --> 02:48.170
so Endeavour can suffer even more.

02:53.100 --> 02:54.400
You'll be able to use it.

02:54.810 --> 02:55.960
Your transformation, I mean.

03:00.220 --> 03:02.940
If the target is someone dear to you,

03:02.940 --> 03:06.320
you can use their Quirk
by drinking the blood.

03:06.970 --> 03:08.780
Before Machia was seized,

03:09.230 --> 03:11.840
I made sure to grab a sample

03:12.430 --> 03:14.240
of Twice's blood.

03:15.710 --> 03:17.290
The sad, sad parade

03:18.440 --> 03:21.500
shall continue with our help.

03:22.350 --> 03:24.010
We will have

03:25.360 --> 03:26.460
the last laugh.

04:54.520 --> 04:58.020
(My Hero Academia Season 7)

05:10.840 --> 05:11.960
Shigaraki...

05:15.850 --> 05:16.720
Are you...

05:29.000 --> 05:30.780
Fear not.

05:31.150 --> 05:34.330
Tomura is making a smooth recovery.

05:35.360 --> 05:39.160
He is overcoming
the Quirk Singularity Theory as we speak.

05:39.850 --> 05:42.460
Is he still Shigaraki?

05:42.880 --> 05:44.700
Yes. Definitely.

05:46.240 --> 05:47.150
Spinner,

05:47.690 --> 05:49.500
I'm pretty sure you know

05:49.500 --> 05:52.010
what proportion of villains

05:52.010 --> 05:53.360
are heteromorphs.

05:54.000 --> 05:57.440
No matter how hard the government
and heroes tried to illuminate the nation,

05:57.440 --> 05:59.480
there were dark corners
where no light could reach.

05:59.840 --> 06:03.930
Plenty of heteromorphs hold
grudges against the so-called heroes.

06:04.620 --> 06:06.220
(Spinner is Our Voice)
Our remnants established the connection.

06:06.220 --> 06:07.210
Our remnants established the connection.

06:07.760 --> 06:09.240
During the League's early days,

06:09.240 --> 06:11.980
you showed yourself to the world.

06:12.490 --> 06:15.230
It began with a wannabe
who copied the outfit.

06:15.230 --> 06:18.330
But that figure is now
the guiding light of many heteromorphs.

06:18.970 --> 06:20.650
That title is too fancy for me.

06:21.180 --> 06:23.340
I'm not fighting for a great cause.

06:24.080 --> 06:25.000
I'm only here because...

06:25.000 --> 06:26.720
The die is cast.

06:27.440 --> 06:28.860
The escaped convicts are a problem.

06:29.230 --> 06:31.340
But rioters are waiting for you.

06:32.490 --> 06:36.250
You must pull the trigger
on Re-Destro's behalf.

06:37.840 --> 06:40.280
The thought of a nobody like me

06:40.700 --> 06:42.680
can't stop this future from unfolding.

06:43.390 --> 06:47.560
The small steps you take
will serve to inspire countless.

06:47.900 --> 06:49.500
Destroy...

06:50.270 --> 06:52.280
I'll destroy everything...

06:54.920 --> 06:56.910
Stop hesitating.

06:58.440 --> 06:59.390
Shigaraki.

07:00.410 --> 07:01.480
I'm only here

07:02.060 --> 07:03.310
for your sake.

07:03.900 --> 07:05.960
That's right, Iguchi.

07:06.410 --> 07:11.290
Everyone can be someone's hero.

07:11.610 --> 07:15.620
(Let You Down)

07:15.620 --> 07:18.120
(U.A. High, Temporary Shelter)

07:28.250 --> 07:29.360
The order came down.

07:29.660 --> 07:30.320
What is it?

07:30.990 --> 07:35.080
You-Know-Who anticipated that
our movements would be restricted.

07:35.820 --> 07:36.700
Fan the flame.

07:36.970 --> 07:40.480
Rally the discontented faction
and drag them into this cause.

07:41.200 --> 07:44.920
U.A. High knows Tomura Shigaraki
will become operational again

07:44.920 --> 07:47.180
in less than a week.

07:47.790 --> 07:50.700
The school is aware of the impending
danger, but keeps it from the people.

07:52.060 --> 07:53.260
Fan the flame.

07:53.690 --> 07:58.830
Make sure Izuku Midoriya can no longer
stay within the walls of that fortress.

08:00.540 --> 08:05.080
We are now part of the party hunting
down the Liberation Front and the League.

08:05.690 --> 08:08.400
Despite arresting
several escaped convicts,

08:08.890 --> 08:12.490
the investigation doesn't
seem to make any progress.

08:14.350 --> 08:16.300
I'm dog-tired.

08:16.560 --> 08:19.280
The search areas are too big.

08:19.280 --> 08:21.470
I expected to see more heroes in action.

08:21.470 --> 08:22.730
The problem is worse than I thought.

08:22.730 --> 08:23.760
Can't agree more.

08:24.010 --> 08:25.610
Time to hit the sack.

08:26.090 --> 08:27.840
Our youth is our strength.

08:28.190 --> 08:31.040
Every action we take is directly
tied to our training and development.

08:31.040 --> 08:33.160
They did tell us to get stronger.

08:33.580 --> 08:34.460
Everybody,

08:34.460 --> 08:36.040
don't forget to brush your teeth.

08:36.440 --> 08:39.630
I was hoping we'd have time to
exchange dirty stories.

08:39.630 --> 08:40.830
That won't be necessary.

08:41.360 --> 08:42.860
But I get it.

08:44.560 --> 08:47.150
I can't wait to take a shower.

08:47.150 --> 08:48.170
Agreed.

08:49.390 --> 08:51.400
We don't even have time to talk.

08:52.480 --> 08:53.660
Please let this place

08:54.330 --> 08:55.630
become

08:56.240 --> 08:59.320
the hero academy where he can stay!

09:01.580 --> 09:03.920
I never got the chance
to properly thank her.

09:05.400 --> 09:06.300
Uraraka...

09:07.360 --> 09:10.560
I'm here, just like every other day!

09:10.910 --> 09:13.070
Sir, you're in good spirits.

09:13.070 --> 09:14.010
It's the total opposite.

09:14.280 --> 09:16.720
Officer Tsukauchi and the Principal too?

09:17.320 --> 09:19.280
Is this about Aoyama?

09:21.210 --> 09:22.780
It's what comes next.

09:23.160 --> 09:26.640
Only a handful of people
know the information.

09:27.850 --> 09:29.980
It's the final plan
for the second final battle.

09:31.150 --> 09:32.700
Now is the time to discuss it.

09:34.260 --> 09:35.200
(The Next Morning)

09:35.200 --> 09:39.230
Attention, all refugees currently
residing within U.A. High.

09:39.950 --> 09:43.050
Based on the joint investigation
conducted by the police and pro heroes,

09:43.050 --> 09:47.560
Tomura Shigaraki,
the villain from the League

09:47.560 --> 09:52.320
who brought an unprecedented catastrophe,
will make a move after four days.

09:52.810 --> 09:56.480
To ensure your safety,

09:56.480 --> 10:00.040
a curfew will be implemented
in U.A. High after four days.

10:00.040 --> 10:04.490
The greatest defence system
we have will go online.

10:05.050 --> 10:08.460
When the evacuation system is active,
there will be inconveniences

10:08.460 --> 10:12.480
and restrictions for everyone.

10:12.480 --> 10:14.940
We look forward to your cooperation.

10:14.940 --> 10:16.880
We will overcome this crisis together.

10:21.000 --> 10:21.880
Everybody,

10:22.750 --> 10:24.700
thank you!

10:25.080 --> 10:27.280
Midoriya, are you going to leave again?

10:27.680 --> 10:28.400
Yes.

10:29.020 --> 10:32.560
It was more than enough time
for me to clean myself of the dust.

10:33.120 --> 10:36.400
Your safety is our top priority.

10:36.810 --> 10:37.930
But remember,

10:38.250 --> 10:43.210
be ready for the evacuation system
that might be activated at any time.

10:43.870 --> 10:45.280
Their honesty is utterly foolish!

10:45.760 --> 10:47.920
They could've defended this place

10:47.920 --> 10:50.140
and given You-Know-Who
a hard time breaking through.

10:50.960 --> 10:54.270
They basically accomplished
our mission for us.

10:54.800 --> 10:58.060
Now, our future is guaranteed.

11:31.680 --> 11:33.400
After leaving U.A. High,

11:33.960 --> 11:37.340
we arrived at a place
30 kilometres away from the school.

11:37.340 --> 11:41.390
It's a new stronghold,
the makeshift fortress known as Troy.

11:42.330 --> 11:46.330
(Makeshift Fortress Troy)
It was completed in a short time thanks to

11:46.330 --> 11:48.350
(Makeshift Fortress Troy)
Cementos, Power Loader, and Ectoplasm.

11:48.860 --> 11:51.420
This isn't U.A. High, but it is a fort.

11:51.870 --> 11:54.600
Take your luggage
to your rooms and get ready.

11:54.600 --> 11:56.960
The design is a homage
to Heights Alliance.

11:56.960 --> 11:58.280
Makes me feel right at home.

11:58.280 --> 12:00.670
Let's hope this isn't
the last we'll ever live.

12:00.670 --> 12:01.580
That's not funny.

12:17.880 --> 12:18.760
Uraraka.

12:18.760 --> 12:20.480
Hey there, Deku.

12:20.480 --> 12:22.010
Did you unpack?

12:22.010 --> 12:22.830
Yeah.

12:22.830 --> 12:24.760
I barely brought anything with me.

12:25.020 --> 12:26.480
I only brought some spare clothes.

12:31.200 --> 12:32.060
Uraraka.

12:32.460 --> 12:33.770
I want to thank you for the other day.

12:34.430 --> 12:36.200
I never got the chance
to properly thank you.

12:36.560 --> 12:37.740
I really appreciate it.

12:37.740 --> 12:39.610
Well... It was nothing.

12:40.040 --> 12:43.080
You are still sweating over
the small things as usual.

12:43.710 --> 12:45.610
What are you doing out here anyway?

12:45.610 --> 12:46.460
Well...

12:47.050 --> 12:49.130
I'm looking at the city.

12:51.040 --> 12:52.140
I guess

12:52.890 --> 12:54.320
I'm pretty weird.

12:54.720 --> 12:55.820
That's not true.

12:55.820 --> 12:58.000
You're strong, brave,
and have a nice hairdo.

12:58.000 --> 12:59.500
You're also very kind and pretty...

12:59.500 --> 13:01.290
No, that's not what I mean.

13:02.720 --> 13:03.760
That day,

13:04.140 --> 13:06.910
when I was shouting
from the top of U.A. High,

13:07.370 --> 13:08.330
the thoughts of

13:08.940 --> 13:11.100
Himiko Toga just poured into my mind.

13:12.640 --> 13:15.960
I fought her alone
when Gigantomachia was rampaging.

13:16.830 --> 13:22.040
I retaliated her ideas
with what I thought was right.

13:22.670 --> 13:25.080
She looked so sad after hearing that.

13:28.060 --> 13:29.560
She is a villain

13:29.930 --> 13:32.830
who destroyed the city, took many lives,
and robbed people of happiness.

13:33.520 --> 13:35.850
It's not a question of forgiving or not.

13:36.200 --> 13:37.210
I understand all that.

13:38.060 --> 13:38.990
But...

13:40.080 --> 13:43.450
I never figured out
what she thinks is natural.

13:43.900 --> 13:48.250
I can't help but think
maybe I know nothing about Himiko Toga.

13:49.520 --> 13:51.390
Which is why I'm looking at the city.

13:52.410 --> 13:55.000
I want to
sear those harrowing views into my memory.

13:55.950 --> 13:58.220
I don't want to be distracted in a fight.

14:00.160 --> 14:01.870
Same here.

14:01.870 --> 14:02.520
Huh?

14:03.240 --> 14:05.100
I saw a weeping little boy

14:05.820 --> 14:08.250
deep inside Shigaraki's heart.

14:09.580 --> 14:11.240
A final battle is inevitable.

14:11.960 --> 14:14.780
But I can't tell myself to ignore
what he hides deep within his heart.

14:19.230 --> 14:20.060
Well,

14:20.600 --> 14:22.410
that makes both of us weirdos.

14:24.430 --> 14:26.380
Thanks for the concerns.

14:27.080 --> 14:27.850
I'm doing all right.

14:28.320 --> 14:30.080
I have a big brother too.

14:30.810 --> 14:33.360
We shouldn't be
comparing our families.

14:34.300 --> 14:35.040
I don't even know

14:35.520 --> 14:37.630
what Toya liked.

14:38.090 --> 14:39.850
Probably udon.

14:39.850 --> 14:41.420
The kind that's burning hot.

14:43.320 --> 14:44.330
In that case,

14:45.530 --> 14:47.100
I'll grab some udon with him.

14:51.760 --> 14:53.130
We must stop them.

14:57.950 --> 14:59.000
(My Hero Academia
Uravity, Ochaco Uraraka)

15:01.960 --> 15:03.000
(My Hero Academia
All For One)

15:04.570 --> 15:07.130
(Three Days Later)
Lies won't work on me.

15:07.720 --> 15:11.660
I can detect
the slightest bit of malicious intent.

15:12.520 --> 15:14.960
What was that Quirk called again?

15:15.420 --> 15:17.870
After all, it was way back
when it all began.

15:18.320 --> 15:21.790
With all the boosts I got,
my memory about it is very vague.

15:23.130 --> 15:26.830
The original owner
was probably a nameless nobody.

15:27.520 --> 15:29.870
His descendants are doing well.

15:30.750 --> 15:32.440
By a fateful chance,

15:32.440 --> 15:36.220
he and All Might had me cornered.

15:37.120 --> 15:38.190
However,

15:38.590 --> 15:41.980
this Quirk will carry me
to victory this time.

15:42.750 --> 15:47.500
Nothing brings me more joy than seeing
the seed I planted bearing fruits.

15:48.600 --> 15:50.400
Yes, nothing has changed.

15:50.400 --> 15:52.400
I'd love to have some fine wine.

15:52.910 --> 15:55.470
It'd better be 40-year-old Macallan.

15:55.920 --> 15:59.100
We have a 16-year-old bottle.
My son can deliver it to you.

15:59.400 --> 16:01.520
Yes. Do send it here.

16:01.960 --> 16:05.820
For that,
I'll need a way to contact your son.

16:06.220 --> 16:08.200
I wouldn't want to take any chances.

16:08.640 --> 16:10.490
Yes. Certainly.

16:10.490 --> 16:13.200
Things are quite nasty out there,
my dear uncle.

16:13.630 --> 16:15.360
Correct. It is chaotic out there.

16:16.040 --> 16:18.970
No lies and malicious intent.
She is clear.

16:19.710 --> 16:21.320
Even if the heroes are casting bait,

16:21.320 --> 16:24.840
I'll still be safe
when the couple is interrogated.

16:25.840 --> 16:29.740
This is the last silly phone call
we make to avoid eavesdropping.

16:30.890 --> 16:32.110
See you tomorrow.

16:32.730 --> 16:35.020
Yes. See you tomorrow.

16:40.860 --> 16:42.200
Let's do this.

16:53.120 --> 16:54.460
Thanks for coming.

16:55.070 --> 16:56.400
Aoyama,

16:56.400 --> 16:57.420
what are you doing here?

16:58.280 --> 16:59.690
Aren't you in the detention centre?

17:00.440 --> 17:02.730
My parents' lawyer got me out.

17:03.260 --> 17:04.490
I'll inform the others.

17:04.490 --> 17:05.550
We are conducting another search.

17:05.550 --> 17:06.410
Wait.

17:07.530 --> 17:09.160
I have something to tell you.

17:13.360 --> 17:14.410
Hilarious, isn't it?

17:14.990 --> 17:16.570
Despite this dysfunctional society,

17:16.910 --> 17:18.750
the judicial system still works.

17:20.540 --> 17:23.390
What is the point in following through
with an idea of the past

17:23.390 --> 17:24.810
in this present world?

17:25.660 --> 17:26.730
Aoyama?

17:27.050 --> 17:30.040
I'll tell you All For One's true motive.

17:31.240 --> 17:33.480
Do you know what the world will be like

17:33.480 --> 17:35.610
after Japan's collapse?

17:36.970 --> 17:39.850
(Nikkei Stock Average)
The value of our currency takes a dive.

17:39.850 --> 17:42.700
(Nikkei Stock Average)
Many local companies have gone bankrupt.

17:43.370 --> 17:45.600
The villains have gone active again
after a rallying call.

17:46.000 --> 17:47.960
The whole world is affected.

17:48.730 --> 17:53.050
The world faces a crisis like the Great
Depression and the Advent of Quirks.

17:54.430 --> 17:56.280
International employment is non-existent.

17:57.040 --> 17:58.540
The loss of faith in our currency.

17:59.050 --> 18:00.280
It's an era of total chaos.

18:00.650 --> 18:03.370
What are you talking about, Aoyama?

18:04.090 --> 18:06.650
Once Japan lacks the ability
to implement long-term policies,

18:07.150 --> 18:09.100
it will scramble for short-term safety.

18:09.100 --> 18:11.090
Constant conflicts will break out.
The nation's economy will wither.

18:12.000 --> 18:13.500
Japan will eventually be abandoned.

18:14.040 --> 18:16.940
The reason is that every nation
wants to prioritise their own interests.

18:18.010 --> 18:19.150
In that world,

18:19.480 --> 18:22.000
imagine a country with a water shortage

18:22.000 --> 18:24.490
stumbling upon a Quirk
that creates drinking water,

18:25.080 --> 18:27.760
electricity, or natural gas.

18:28.890 --> 18:31.640
As the world is plunged into total chaos,

18:32.140 --> 18:34.600
we are shaping
an arena for a special figure

18:34.600 --> 18:37.680
to seize total control over everyone.

18:38.590 --> 18:41.080
He will become the overlord of the world.

18:41.760 --> 18:44.360
It can be done
by tipping the balance somewhere,

18:45.320 --> 18:47.050
and how it's done doesn't even matter.

18:47.840 --> 18:49.930
That doesn't sound right.

18:50.320 --> 18:52.200
The world will never allow that.

18:53.130 --> 18:53.950
Besides,

18:55.400 --> 18:57.210
we are still standing.

18:58.220 --> 18:59.070
Yeah.

18:59.500 --> 19:02.750
Which is why this is the last end for us.

19:03.790 --> 19:04.640
Sorry.

19:05.180 --> 19:06.280
I still end up

19:06.750 --> 19:08.960
wanting to protect my parents.

19:09.870 --> 19:11.690
All For One!

19:12.060 --> 19:15.470
Well done, Yuga Aoyama.

19:15.880 --> 19:18.970
You must be terrified
when you betrayed your friends.

19:19.280 --> 19:22.960
Their trust must feel like torture.

19:23.770 --> 19:25.610
I'm surprised you made it through.

19:26.410 --> 19:30.060
You did a splendid job
explaining my ultimate goals.

19:30.060 --> 19:32.170
Even though it wasn't exactly correct.

19:32.680 --> 19:34.940
Did you get that from your parents?

19:35.600 --> 19:36.280
Yes...

19:36.720 --> 19:37.880
They say you guarantee

19:38.190 --> 19:40.750
we can live happily
in the new world you create.

19:40.750 --> 19:42.570
I believed you!

19:43.470 --> 19:46.460
The pain I'm feeling at this moment

19:47.280 --> 19:48.870
(Flash)
is immeasurable, uncle!

19:51.770 --> 19:53.400
Cursed ingrate.

19:54.460 --> 19:56.620
Terrific acting, Aoyama.

19:56.620 --> 19:57.960
It can't be helped.

19:57.960 --> 20:00.350
We need to lure him out, right?

20:00.350 --> 20:02.910
Your acting wasn't too shabby either.

20:02.910 --> 20:04.700
It was a ruse to lure him out.

20:04.700 --> 20:06.940
But seeing your tears
makes me want to get serious.

20:06.940 --> 20:09.080
I didn't just wet my eyes.

20:09.080 --> 20:11.100
I think I wet myself!

20:11.100 --> 20:13.040
Great work, Aoyama.

20:13.600 --> 20:15.480
For the sake of my parents,

20:15.930 --> 20:18.780
for everyone and for myself,

20:20.060 --> 20:22.430
I want to fight All For One!

20:23.920 --> 20:25.340
Such a disappointment.

20:26.670 --> 20:28.220
What is going on here?

20:29.390 --> 20:30.920
I'll lure him out.

20:30.920 --> 20:32.320
I can do it anytime you want.

20:32.830 --> 20:36.920
I didn't detect
any lies or malicious intent

20:36.920 --> 20:38.960
from my phone calls
with him and his parents.

20:39.450 --> 20:40.880
How did he...

20:42.110 --> 20:43.130
No,

20:43.130 --> 20:44.410
it matters not now.

20:45.180 --> 20:49.520
Trap or not, One For All
is standing right here for me to take.

20:50.380 --> 20:54.570
My "Search" can locate a target
I've seen and show me their weakness.

20:55.040 --> 21:00.760
The heroes Tomura encountered in the last
battle are scattered around the nation.

21:00.760 --> 21:03.580
They won't make it here in time.

21:04.300 --> 21:06.830
That is precisely
why I could bring my people near you

21:06.830 --> 21:09.600
without anyone noticing.

21:10.600 --> 21:13.980
There's nothing
you can do in this situation.

21:15.400 --> 21:16.700
All For One...

21:17.800 --> 21:19.070
Kurogiri?

21:19.530 --> 21:21.210
How did they make him act?

21:21.980 --> 21:25.100
But that saves me some trouble...

21:26.750 --> 21:28.800
My parents told me

21:30.320 --> 21:33.040
the one thing
All For One hates the most

21:33.760 --> 21:36.760
is letting the world know
there is still hope for Japan,

21:37.660 --> 21:39.710
that we might unite the whole world

21:40.320 --> 21:43.200
with the light and hope
that comes with rebuilding our future.

21:44.080 --> 21:45.120
Today,

21:46.320 --> 21:48.330
we will defeat you!

23:20.990 --> 23:22.170
Next episode.

23:22.840 --> 23:26.330
The final battle between the heroes
and the villains has begun.

23:27.690 --> 23:30.860
The heroes devise a plan
to isolate the villains.

23:30.860 --> 23:33.070
Aoyama played a pivotal role in this plan,

23:33.560 --> 23:36.000
so did Shinso with his Quirk, Brainwash,

23:36.570 --> 23:38.570
and Monoma's Quirk, Copy.

23:39.580 --> 23:42.760
We will make this plan work.

23:43.920 --> 23:45.440
Next episode, "Division".

23:46.200 --> 23:47.630
(Next episode: Division)
Go beyond.

23:47.630 --> 23:49.940
(Next episode: Division)
Plus Ultra.
